      "level": 1,
      "content": "Append Element to an Empty Linked List"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The code we discussed for appending to a linked list does not work if the linked list is empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If you recall the LinkedList class we introduced in the previous lesson, its head attribute is initially set to None."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "class LinkedList:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.head = None"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This means that the head attribute of an empty linked list is None."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Therefore, to append a new node to an empty linked list, we will simply set head to point to new_node."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "if not self.head:\n    self.head = new_node\n    return"
    },
